{%- comment -%}
  Closing or draw date, written the way an entrant reads it.

  "Closing today" / "Closing tomorrow" are calendar comparisons in the shop's
  timezone, not fuzzy countdowns, and they only ever reflect a real date held in
  custom.closing_at. No date, no output.

  A DATE THAT HAS PASSED PRODUCES NO OUTPUT AT ALL.

  It used to render "Closed". That was the one thing this snippet must never
  say, because a passed date does not close anything: Shopify closes a
  competition when its inventory runs out, and a competition past its published
  date with entries left is still on sale. Printing "Closed" above a working
  Enter button told the customer the opposite of what the page would let them
  do. Saying nothing is honest; the entry form is the answer to "can I enter".

  The same applies to draw_at: a draw date in the past is a date that has been
  and gone, not a state this line can describe.

  With `detail: true` the label also carries the closing *time* and how many days
  away it is. A deadline a customer has to work out for themselves is a deadline
  that does not influence the decision: "Closes Wed 23 Sep" leaves them to check
  a calendar, and says nothing about whether entries stop at 9am or midnight.
  Both facts are already in the metafield — this states them rather than
  implying pressure. Nothing here counts down and nothing is invented: if the
  merchant stored no time, no time is shown.

  Parameters:
    product  (required)
    field    'closing_at' (default) or 'draw_at'
    icon     show a clock icon (default true)
    detail   add the time and the days remaining (default false, so cards stay
             compact and only the competition page carries the long form)
{%- endcomment -%}

{%- liquid
  assign which = field | default: 'closing_at'
  if which == 'draw_at'
    assign stamp = product.metafields.custom.draw_at.value
  else
    assign stamp = product.metafields.custom.closing_at.value
  endif

  comment
    Nothing is rendered for a date that has already passed. See the note above.
  endcomment
  assign is_future = false
  if stamp != blank
    assign now_epoch = 'now' | date: '%s' | times: 1
    assign stamp_epoch = stamp | date: '%s' | times: 1
    if stamp_epoch > now_epoch
      assign is_future = true
    endif
  endif
-%}

{%- if is_future -%}
  {%- liquid
    assign today = 'now' | date: '%Y-%m-%d'
    assign tomorrow = 'now' | date: '%s' | plus: 86400 | date: '%Y-%m-%d'
    assign target_day = stamp | date: '%Y-%m-%d'

    comment
      A merchant who set only a date gets midnight, which is a storage artefact
      rather than a stated cut-off. Showing "at 12:00 am" would present it as
      one, so the time is only shown when it is genuinely a time of day.
    endcomment
    assign clock = stamp | date: '%H%M'
    assign has_time = true
    if clock == '0000'
      assign has_time = false
    endif
    assign time_text = stamp | date: '%-I:%M %p' | downcase

    assign label = ''
    if target_day == today
      if which == 'draw_at'
        assign label = 'products.competition.draw_today' | t
      else
        assign label = 'products.competition.closing_today' | t
      endif
      if detail and has_time
        assign label = 'products.competition.at_time' | t: label: label, time: time_text
      endif
    elsif target_day == tomorrow
      if which == 'draw_at'
        assign label = 'products.competition.draw_tomorrow' | t
      else
        assign label = 'products.competition.closing_tomorrow' | t
      endif
      if detail and has_time
        assign label = 'products.competition.at_time' | t: label: label, time: time_text
      endif
    else
      assign formatted = stamp | date: '%a %-d %b'
      if which == 'draw_at'
        assign prefix = 'products.competition.draw_date' | t
      else
        assign prefix = 'products.competition.closes' | t
      endif
      assign label = prefix | append: ' ' | append: formatted

      if detail
        if has_time
          assign label = 'products.competition.at_time' | t: label: label, time: time_text
        endif

        comment
          Whole calendar days, so a deadline late tomorrow does not round down
          to zero days the way a raw seconds division would.
        endcomment
        assign today_epoch = today | date: '%s' | times: 1
        assign target_epoch = target_day | date: '%s' | times: 1
        assign days_away = target_epoch | minus: today_epoch | divided_by: 86400

        if days_away > 1
          assign away_text = 'products.competition.days_away' | t: count: days_away
          assign label = label | append: ' · ' | append: away_text
        endif
      endif
    endif
  -%}
  <span class="competition-meta__item">
    {%- unless icon == false -%}{%- render 'icon', icon: 'clock', size: 14 -%}{%- endunless -%}
    <time datetime="{{ stamp | date: '%Y-%m-%dT%H:%M:%S%z' }}">{{ label }}</time>
  </span>
{%- endif -%}
